# Adrian Martikov, Davian's eldest son (docs/voice/adrian_martikov.md). He was the raven that walked beside the party
# on the Svalich road (svalich_road/events:ravens).
# first_meeting: at the foot of the lane, once (approach). start: at the camp, then in the fermenting hall once the
# winery is the family's again.

~ first_meeting
set adrian_met
Narrator: A raven drops out of the dead vines onto the lane ahead of you, hops twice, and unfolds into a lean, black-eyed man who brushes feathers off his sleeves as if they were crumbs.
if flag.raven_fed
Adrian: You fed me a crust on the Svalich road. It was stale. I've had worse from family. Adrian Martikov. That's twice now you haven't shot me, which in this valley is practically a friendship.
elif flag.raven_harmed
Adrian [angry]: You knocked me into a ditch on the Svalich road. The wing still clicks when I fly. Adrian Martikov. I'm only talking to you because we're short of choices.
else
Adrian: Strangers on our lane, upright and armed. Either you're lost or you're the help. Adrian Martikov. Please be the help.
endif
if flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met
Adrian: My brother Urwin sent word ahead of you from Vallaki. The bird arrived exhausted and full of your names. Urwin never could write a short letter.
endif
Adrian: Don't walk up the lane yet. The vines are awake, and they're not ours anymore. My father's at our camp under the trees. He'll want to look at you before you get yourselves killed on his property.
* Take us to your father. -> to_father
* What do you mean, the vines are awake? -> vines
* [if flag.raven_harmed] About the raven. We're sorry. -> apology

~ vines
Adrian: The druids from Yester Hill grow things. Blights, they call them: brush and thorn that walks about and has opinions. They've planted them all down the rows. Go up the lane and the vineyard stands up to meet you.
-> first_menu

~ first_menu
* Take us to your father. -> to_father
* [if flag.raven_harmed and not flag.adrian_apology_heard] About the raven. We're sorry. -> apology

~ apology
set adrian_apology_heard
Adrian: Sorry. Well. It was dark, I was a bird, and this valley teaches people to hit birds. I'll take sorry. My father won't, so don't spend all of it on me.
-> first_menu

~ to_father
Adrian: This way, round by the trees. Mind the brambles. They're only brambles. Probably.
interject tag:curious: You were the raven. On the road. You walked beside us for a mile.
Adrian: A mile and a half. You walk slowly.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- At the camp, later in the hall

~ start
if flag.winery_reclaimed
Adrian: Back in my own hall, scrubbing druid out of my own vats. You'd be amazed what they left in the mash. No, you wouldn't. You met it.
else
Adrian: Father's by the fire, Stefania's everywhere at once, and I'm here, being useful at a distance. What do you need?
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* What happened here? -> what_happened
* [if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.adrian_side_heard] Stefania told us about Elvir. -> elvir
* [if flag.adrian_side_heard and not flag.adrian_told_order and not flag.elvir_truth_known] [Insight DC 13] There's more to it than "I flew." -> elvir_insight | elvir_insight_fail
* [if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.adrian_truth_shared] We found what Elvir scratched into his cage. -> elvir_truth
* [if flag.davian_met and not flag.yester_hill_resolved] Come with us to Yester Hill. -> come_along
* [if flag.winery_reclaimed] How's the wine? -> wine
* Goodbye. -> END

~ what_happened
Adrian: Three months ago the druids came up the lane at dusk with half the forest walking behind them. We fought a while. Then Father said fly, so we flew. They've been pulling up our floors ever since.
Adrian: Looking for the last stone. Father hid it the night we ran, and he won't tell me where. He tells Stefania things. Ask her why; I've stopped.
-> menu

~ elvir
set adrian_side_heard
Adrian: Then you know what Father thinks. Last spring he sent Elvir and me to watch the hill. The druids' things caught us in the bracken. I flew. Elvir didn't. That's all there is.
interject tag:blunt: That isn't all there is. That's the part you say out loud.
Adrian: It's the part that's true.
-> menu

~ elvir_insight
set adrian_told_order
Narrator: He's looking at his hands. Not the way a man looks at hands that ran away; the way a man looks at hands that did as they were told.
Adrian: ...A root had him round the leg and a thorn right through it. He couldn't change. He told me to fly for Father, in Father's own voice. So I went. When we came back there was only blood on the bracken.
Adrian: I've never told Father. It sounds like an excuse. Maybe it is one.
-> menu

~ elvir_insight_fail
Narrator: He meets your eye, shrugs, and goes back to the cask he's scraping. Whatever else there is, he has kept it a year, and he's had the practice.
-> menu

~ elvir_truth
set adrian_truth_shared
Adrian [sad]: "I sent him." He wrote that? With what, his fingernails? ...Of course he did. He was the stubborn one. Everyone else in this family thinks it was me who decides things.
Adrian: Tell Father. Not me; he won't hear it from me. From you he might.
-> menu

~ come_along
if flag.raven_harmed and not flag.adrian_apology_heard
Adrian: With the people who put me in a ditch? ...Yes. Fine. I've wanted to see that hill burn for a year, and you're the only ones going.
else
Adrian: I've wanted to go back up that hill for a year. I kept waiting for someone to ask so I could say no. It turns out I can't.
endif
if not flag.winery_reclaimed
Adrian: Father will say the house comes first. Father is usually right about houses. He's wrong about other things.
endif
join adrian_martikov
set adrian_went_to_hill
interject class:cleric: You know there may be... remains. Up there.
Adrian: That's why I'm going.
-> END

~ wine
if flag.winery_stones_returned >= 2
Adrian: The vines put out new leaves overnight. Green ones. I stood in the rows at dawn and wept like a child, and if you tell anyone I'll seal you in a cask.
elif flag.winery_stones_returned >= 1
Adrian: One stone in the soil and the vines remember what they're for. It'll be thin this year. Thin is better than dead.
else
Adrian: Without the stones it's grape juice with ambitions. We need them back in the ground.
endif
if flag.martikovs_reconciled
Adrian: Father's given me the press. He says his knees are finished with it. His knees are fine. It's the kindest lie he's ever told.
endif
-> menu
